{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause, measured 2026-11-04 on origin/main 30f06afc412 (macOS host, load average 28-36).\n\nBaseline: the benchmark test run alone took 310.0 s wall (user 17.8 s, sys 31.0 s), rc=1 at the 300 s timeout. The timeout stack was in the per-comment cross-session read (`emit_cross_session_warning` -> `show_ticket` -> reduce).\n\nGit child processes by caller, `rebar.import_tickets` with n=50 tickets, 1 comment each:\n- Acting session id set (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, as in any agent shell): 120 git processes, 15.8 s wall. 100 of them are 2 per comment, both in `ensure_fresh` under the warning's `show_ticket`: `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (repo_root_or_none) and `git rev-parse --verify <branch>`.\n- No session id (all 4 session vars unset, as in CI): 19 git processes, 3.2 s wall. `cross_session_warning_for` returns before the read when no session id is set.\n\nThat is why CI passes in about 21 s and local agent shells time out: CI's workflow sets none of REBAR_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, OPENCODE_SESSION_ID, or SESSION_ID.\n\nWhy the per-comment check exists: story recent-wholesome-fulmar (6d95718080c, 2026-08-28) added `emit_cross_session_warning` to each single-ticket public library call (`comment`, `edit_ticket`, `link`, `set_file_impact`, ...) for direct `import rebar` callers. It explicitly keeps bulk operations silent and has outer surfaces hold `suppress_cross_session_warning()` so they advise once. `import_tickets` was not considered; it reuses those public single-ticket calls internally, so it inherited one detector read per row.\n\nThe check is redundant inside import:\n- Every ticket the import's passes 2a-2d touch was created by this same import in pass 1. A new ticket has no claimed_session; statuses are replayed later, in pass 2e, through `transition_compute`, which does not emit. Push is deferred until the end of the import.\n- The CLI path (`rebar store import`) already runs under `suppress_cross_session_warning()` (`_cli/_execute.py`), and `import` is not in the CLI's cross-session allowlist; MCP tools are wrapped the same way. Only direct library callers pay the per-row read.\n\nFix: `import_tickets` holds `suppress_cross_session_warning()` across its write passes, the same guard the CLI and MCP surfaces already hold. Single-ticket library calls outside import keep their warning unchanged. No opcert code touched."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793793813039225001,"uuid":"eea00abc-74d6-4014-9253-104ca12b951f"}